    "hook": [
     "A whole book of the Bible is a love song, and the woman sings most of it."
    ],
    "setting": [
     "The book calls itself “Solomon’s Song of Songs” (",
     {
      "r": "SNG.1.1",
      "t": "Song of Songs 1:1"
     },
     "), a Hebrew way of saying the finest of songs. Three voices sing: a woman, the man she loves, and a group called the daughters of Jerusalem. God’s name does not plainly appear."
    ],
    "limit": [
     "The Song celebrates love; it does not give rules for every relationship. How far it also pictures God and His people is a question faithful Baptists answer in two ways."
    ],
